###  http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#VisualMaterial
:VisualMaterial rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:subClassOf :Dimension ;
                :dimensionIndex 1 ;
                :promptExtractionText "Extract Visual Material elements from the image. Visual Material includes: people, objects, characters, scenes, graphics, and any salient visual elements. For each visual element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'smiling_girl', 'burning_house'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the smiling girl', 'the burning house'), 3) A brief description of what you see. Focus on clearly visible, distinct visual elements that are important to understanding the meme. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"smiling_girl\", \"label\": \"the smiling girl\", \"description\": \"A young girl with a mischievous smile in the foreground\"}"@en ;
                :prototypicalQuestions """1. What visual elements are present in this meme? (Identify all images, graphics, illustrations, photographs, symbols, or visual components)

2. What is the source or origin of the visual content? (Consider whether images are from movies, TV shows, stock photos, original artwork, screenshots, etc.)

3. How are the visual elements composed and arranged within the frame? (Examine layout, positioning, size relationships, and visual balance)

4. What colors, lighting, and visual style characterize the meme? (Analyze color schemes, contrast, brightness, saturation, and overall aesthetic)

5. What emotions or reactions do the visual elements convey? (Consider facial expressions, body language, visual mood, and atmospheric qualities)

6. Are there recognizable people, characters, objects, or settings in the visuals? (Identify any familiar faces, fictional characters, locations, or iconic imagery)

7. What visual techniques or effects have been applied? (Look for editing, filters, distortion, overlays, scaling, or other modifications)

8. How do the visual elements relate to each other within the meme? (Examine visual connections, contrasts, parallels, or interactions between different visual components)

9. What cultural or symbolic meanings are embedded in the visual content? (Consider visual metaphors, symbolic representations, or culturally significant imagery)

10. How do the visual elements support or create the meme's intended message? (Analyze how the imagery contributes to humor, commentary, or communicative purpose)""" ;
                rdfs:comment "Visual Material includes: people, objects, characters, scenes, graphics, and any salient visual elements."@en ;
                rdfs:label "Visual Material"@en .


